# MadGraph5 batch script: p p > e+ e- j at LO with MLM matching switched on.
# built-by: validation/madgraph/gen_mlm_references.sh
#
# The single-multiplicity MLM reference. With one jet multiplicity the
# composite integrand is not needed, so the xqcut cut, the two setclscales
# calls per point and the rewgt alpha_s / PDF factors can each be compared
# against MadEvent before mixed multiplicities exist on this side.
#
# The run card is pp_to_llj_dyn's (13 TeV, lhaid 247000, mmll = 50, the
# dynamical kT-clustering scale) with four lines added:
#
#   - ickkw = 1, xqcut = 20: MadEvent's matching mode. xqcut > 0 rewrites
#     ptj and mmjj to xqcut (auto_ptj_mjj) and zeroes drjj / drjl in setcuts.f;
#     ickkw = 1 makes setclscales keep going past the pure-cut early return and
#     makes rewgt multiply the alpha_s and PDF ratios into every event.
#   - vector_size = 1: the scalar path. On the vector path SCALUP reads the
#     lowered matrix-element PDF scale rather than q2bck (auto_dsig_v4.inc),
#     so a reference taken there records a different event header.
#   - systematics_program = none: use_syst stays on, so each event still
#     carries its <mgrwt> block (the rewgt vertex scales and the PDF-ratio
#     chain as MadEvent itself wrote them), but the post-run reweighting pass
#     that would rewrite the event file with scale / PDF variations is not run.
#     It changes neither the cross section nor the parton-level events.
generate p p > e+ e- j
output pp_to_llj_mlm -nojpeg
launch
  set ebeam1 6500
  set ebeam2 6500
  set fixed_ren_scale False
  set fixed_fac_scale1 False
  set fixed_fac_scale2 False
  set scale 91.188
  set dsqrt_q2fact1 91.188
  set dsqrt_q2fact2 91.188
  set dynamical_scale_choice -1
  set pdlabel1 lhapdf
  set pdlabel2 lhapdf
  set lhaid 247000
  set mmll 50
  set ickkw 1
  set xqcut 20
  set vector_size 1
  set systematics_program none
  done
